+# Airflow 3.3.2 Deployment Checklist
+
+**DAG:** `inventory_snapshot`  
+**Upgrade Path:** 2.11.2 → 3.3.2  
+**Date:** 2026-09-30
+
+---
+
+## Pre-Deployment
+
+- [ ] **Review Changes**
+  - Read `UPGRADE_3.3_NOTES.md`
+  - Understand the breaking changes in Airflow 3.3
+  - Confirm no other DAGs in your environment need similar upgrades
+
+- [ ] **Environment Setup**
+  - Ensure your Airflow cluster is running or will be updated to 3.3.2
+  - Confirm venv is set to Python 3.8+ (required for Airflow 3.3)
+  - Back up current Airflow configuration and metadata DB (if applicable)
+
+- [ ] **Dependency Installation**
+  ```bash
+  pip install -r requirements.txt  # Installs apache-airflow==3.3.2
+  ```
+
+---
+
+## Deployment
+
+- [ ] **Airflow Upgrade**
+  ```bash
+  # Update Airflow installation
+  pip install --upgrade apache-airflow==3.3.2
+  
+  # Upgrade metadata database schema (if running a shared Airflow instance)
+  airflow db migrate
+  
+  # Verify installation
+  airflow version  # Should show: 3.3.2
+  ```
+
+- [ ] **Service Restart**
+  ```bash
+  # Stop services
+  systemctl stop airflow-scheduler
+  systemctl stop airflow-webserver
+  
+  # Start services
+  systemctl start airflow-scheduler
+  systemctl start airflow-webserver
+  
+  # Check logs for errors
+  tail -f /var/log/airflow/scheduler.log
+  tail -f /var/log/airflow/webserver.log
+  ```
+
+- [ ] **DAG Deployment**
+  - Copy upgraded `dags/inventory_snapshot.py` to your DAGs folder
+  - Copy `requirements.txt` (updated version)
+  - Copy `UPGRADE_3.3_NOTES.md` for team reference
